            "review_title": "Review at Izakaya Totoya",
            "review_text": "Ontourwiththeworld\nLondon\n24 contributions\n0\nDisappointing Experience\nJan 2025 • Friends\nI visited this yesterday, and unfortunately, my experience was a total letdown. Despite the bustling atmosphere, which initially seemed promising, the food and service fell far short of expectations.\nThe menu appeared extensive and appealing, but the reality was disappointing. The seafood fried rice was lukewarm, and the yaki tori was cold, clearly having been prepared well in advance and left to sit. The sausage was also cold, suggesting a lack of attention to food temperature and timing.\nWhat was even more disappointing was the service recovery, or rather, the lack thereof. When we brought the issue to the staff's attention, they seemed unconcerned and unapologetic. They initially refused to remove the cold food from the bill, which was staggering. Their reasoning that we should pay for the yaki tori because we had taken a bite was illogical and unfair. How are customers supposed to know if the food is hot without tasting it? It's not like we would touch the food with our hands first to check the temperature.\nThe staff's insistence on charging us for the cold food was a clear indication of their poor customer service skills and lack of empathy. If they had handled the situation differently, perhaps with an apology and a willingness to correct their mistakes, the experience might have been salvaged. However, their attitude and behavior only added to our frustration.\nTo make matters worse, there were customers smoking inside the restaurant, which is supposed to be banned in public indoor spaces in Vietnam. This blatant disregard for the law and customer well-being is unacceptable.\nIn conclusion, my experience at this restaurant was a disaster. The combination of poor food quality, inadequate service, and blatant disregard for customer comfort and safety makes me question how this establishment remains in business. Unless significant changes are made, I would strongly advise potential customers to avoid this restaurant at all costs.\nRead more\nWritten January 30, 2025",
